# Foundation Uno — publication hygiene.
#
# At U00 there is no application and no build output. These rules exist to keep the
# PUBLIC repository free of private authority, task scratch, credentials and build
# products that later stages will produce. An ignore rule screens a path from Git; it
# never deletes, moves or rewrites a file.

# --- Owner-installed work order: PRIVATE, never published -------------------
# The governing work order is installed by the Owner in the project root. It is
# read-only to implementation agents and must never appear in git ls-files or in a
# pushed commit. The whole WIP folder is screened so no order draft can escape.
/.documents/WIP/workorder-active.md
/.documents/WIP/
/workorder-active.md

# --- Agent task scratch and disposable local evidence ----------------------
/.temp/

# --- Node.js / pnpm / Next.js build products ------------------------------
/node_modules/
/.pnpm-store/
/.next/
/out/
/build/
/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
/.vercel/

# --- Task logs, transient files and local diagnostics ---------------------
*.log
/tmp/
*.tmp

# --- Credentials, keys and environment -----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/.npmrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.keystore

# --- OS and editor noise -------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
